From 3b141518a0b53bfe8bac1469460338975410bd5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:09:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Games] Show achievement sets, missable achievements and
 Beaten progress

RetroAchievements games can have subsets, such as bonus sets, beside their
own set, and mark achievements as missable or as needed to beat the game.
Kodi was told none of it.

Game API 8.5.0 adds RCOnAchievementSets(), which tells Kodi a game's sets
and each achievement's set and type, and RCSetAchievementSetEnabled(),
which turns a set on or off. The achievements dialog shows one set at a
time, switched with a controller's bumpers, marks missable achievements and
the ones beating the game takes, and shows how close the set is to being
beaten. A subset can be turned off there, and stays off.

(cherry picked from commit 451a27550e2a8ed931704f4d5348baff40acf874)
